    "name": null,
    "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/21f3000759/{size}/23528_2.png",
    "excerpt": "<p>Hello <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/23f2004000\">@23f2004000</a>,</p>\n<p>You can practice the commands on the course vm itself. Linux commands don’t work on Windows command prompt. For learning purpose, it is recommended to install Linux, if you know how to dual boot your system or you can install wsl (Windows Subsystem for Linux) or use a VMware.</p>\n<p>Here is a reference link for installing wsl - <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Install WSL | Microsoft Learn</a></p>\n<p>The same is also mentioned in Week 1.1 lecture.</p>\n<p>Thanks &amp; Regards,<br>\nSwati Jain</p>",
    "accepter_name": null,
    "accepter_username": "21f3000759"
